---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro"
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro"
const sponsorUrl = "https://github.com/sponsors/CYXWIZ-Lab"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sponsor"
  description="CyxCode is independent and open source. Sponsorship funds the build, the pattern library, and the roadmap."
  path="/sponsor"
>
  <section class="page-hero reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Support the project</p>
    <h1>Sponsor CyxCode.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      CyxCode is an independent, open-source fork built by a small team. Sponsorship keeps development
      steady, the pattern library growing, and the roadmap honest.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn cta" href={sponsorUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Become a sponsor →</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/code3hr/cyxcode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Star on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band">
    <SectionHeading kicker="Where it goes" title="What sponsorship funds" />
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Pattern library</h3>
        <p>Curation, testing, and community pack infrastructure for the 136+ built-in patterns and learned additions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Core development</h3>
        <p>Continuous work on shell mode, memory, recall, dream consolidation, and behavior versioning.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Infra & releases</h3>
        <p>Build pipelines, signed binaries across platforms, and the release tooling behind <code>/update</code>.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Documentation</h3>
        <p>Docs, guides, and examples that make deterministic recovery approachable for new users.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Community</h3>
        <p>Issue triage, pull request review, and the contributor onboarding that keeps the fork healthy.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature reveal">
        <h3>Long-term direction</h3>
        <p>The roadmap — semantic recall depth, behavior versioning maturity, and beyond.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band">
    <SectionHeading kicker="Why it matters" title="Independent by design" />
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <p style="line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)">
        CyxCode is a fork of <a class="text-link" href="https://opencode.ai" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">OpenCode</a>
        with a specific thesis: <strong style="color:var(--text)">known errors should never cost tokens twice</strong>.
        That idea needs deeper integration than a plugin allows — tool-aware routing, shell metadata, and a learned
        pattern layer that owns its own control plane.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)">
        Sponsorship is the difference between a side project and a tool you can rely on. Every sponsor makes the
        next release sooner and the next pattern more likely to be there when you hit it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band">
    <div class="panel panel--accent closing-cta reveal">
      <div>
        <h2>Back the build.</h2>
        <p>Help CyxCode catch the next error before the LLM ever sees it.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn cta" href={sponsorUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sponsor on GitHub →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .page-hero .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  code {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--mint);
    background: rgba(36, 209, 163, 0.1);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .closing-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 2.5rem;
  }
  .closing-cta p { color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .closing-cta { padding: 1.75rem; }
  }
</style>
